{
  "title": "DB: CHECK constraints for status-like TEXT columns and paired fields",
  "description": "Columns that encode states with nothing enforcing the set or the pairing: step_outputs success/error (baseline 232-243), mirrored by ramekin-core StepResult's success: bool + error: Option (pipeline/step.rs:32-47), which could be a Result-like enum; output_hash = '' as the 'stored inline' sentinel (scraping/output_store.rs:100-114); sessions.token_type (baseline 26-33; string compare in auth/middleware.rs:80); recipe_versions.version_source (set from normalize.rs:35-39 and literals like 'user' in api/recipes/create.rs:104); recipes deleted_at/deleted_seq (deleted_seq set only by the recipes_stamp_delete trigger); shopping_list_history undoes_id/undone_by_id, whose update (api/shopping_list/history.rs:252-255) also lacks WHERE undone_by_id IS NULL and relies on the same transaction's 'already undone' check. \
Check prod rows against each constraint before adding it; backfill, never delete. \
Found in the 2026-11-07 implicit-state-machine audit; line numbers are as of e94669d4ca, so re-check each point before fixing.",
